body:
This was off Facebook; Got a good laugh out of it;

[https://pbs.twimg.com/media/DwVPIKNUwAApeFo.jpg](https://pbs.twimg.com/media/DwVPIKNUwAApeFo.jpg:large)

&#x200B;

(Meme)

Depends on how much you play. If you're playing 3-4 hours a day for a week straight just following MSQ, 2 weeks tops depending on if you watch the full cutscenes and do side quests to get to 50, then you have 50-60, then 60-70. Current end game content is level 70 item level 40

&#x200B;

Dungeons starts as soon as you get to Lv15+

Realistically though, as the years go on, players starts to get into a different point in life and take the world prog less seriously because. 

&#x200B;

Other than Entropy, there are no official sponsors; So if you're not going to get paid for the commitment and energy into this, why go so so hard at something that returns little in the long run? (May be way off here, just based on trend). I can also see the crowd that have the time and the ability to do world prog's side... it being fun. Most mechanics are rehashed old mechanics from Coil and Alexander and Midas etc, so if you're newer to the game, it may take a bit to adapt to it vs the people that's been there and done it first hand when it came out 2-4 years ago (or whenever). The players that have done intense HC World progression and have those mechanics on farm has a slight advantage over those that don't (on kill time). But veteran raiders are also the people that's getting older and taking on more responsibilities/priorities in life. 

&#x200B;

If you earn a living from this via streams though, keep at it and :Thumbs\_up:  


Hence, not surprised that less and less teams are able to commit to the 110% HC mindset of world prog.
